.TH START-MU2E-RUNDB-VIEWER 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-runlog-db t01.00.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
start-mu2e-rundb-viewer \- bootstrap, migrate and start the run-log viewer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B start\-mu2e\-rundb\-viewer
.SH DESCRIPTION
Starts the Django run-log viewer from the checkout that contains the script.
It performs, in order:
.IP 1. 4
Runs
.BR bootstrap\-mu2e\-rundb\-viewer (1),
which creates
.I .venv/
if needed and runs
.B pip install \-\-upgrade
against PyPI.
The script runs under
.BR "set \-euo pipefail" ,
so a host without PyPI access cannot start the viewer.
.IP 2. 4
If
.I .runserver.pid
names a live process, prints a message and exits 0; a stale PID file is
removed.
.IP 3. 4
Exports
.B DJANGO_ENV
(default
.BR development )
and
.BR DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE=runlogdb.settings .
.IP 4. 4
Runs
.B manage.py migrate
on every start.
On PostgreSQL the
.B runs
app is skipped by
.IR runlogdb/db_router.py ,
but Django's own tables (auth, sessions, sites, allauth) are created in the
same database.
.IP 5. 4
Starts the server.
With
.B DJANGO_ENV=production
it runs gunicorn with 4 workers,
.B \-\-daemon
and
.BR "\-\-pid .runserver.pid" ;
otherwise Django's
.B runserver \-\-noreload
in the background with output to
.IR .runserver.log .
If
.I /.dockerenv
exists the server is
.BR exec ed
in the foreground instead.
.PP
.B DJANGO_ENV is decided here, not in .env.
The script exports
.B DJANGO_ENV=development
when the variable is not already in its environment.
.I runlogdb/settings.py
loads
.I .env
with python-dotenv, which does not override variables that are already set,
so a
.B DJANGO_ENV=production
line in
.I .env
is ignored.
The result is development mode: authentication disabled, every request
logged in as the superuser
.BR dev ,
.BR DEBUG ,
.B ALLOWED_HOSTS
.BR * ,
and a local SQLite database.
Export
.B DJANGO_ENV=production
in the calling environment to get production mode.
.SH OPTIONS
None.
Arguments are accepted and ignored.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DJANGO_ENV
.B development
(default) or
.BR production .
Selects the server and the
.IR config/ "<DJANGO_ENV>" .yaml
overlay.
.TP
.B RUNLOGDB_HOST
Bind address, default
.BR 127.0.0.1 .
Read by the shell only; a value in
.I .env
has no effect.
.TP
.B RUNLOGDB_PORT
Bind port, default
.BR 8000 .
Also read by the discovery responder in
.IR runs/apps.py .
Read by the shell; a value in
.I .env
is seen by the responder but not by the server.
.PP
All
.B RUNLOGDB_*
settings variables are described in
.BR mu2edaq\-runlog\-db.yaml (5).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .venv/
Virtual environment created by the bootstrap script.
.TP
.I .runserver.pid
PID of the gunicorn master or the runserver process.
.TP
.I .runserver.log
runserver output (development mode, outside Docker).
gunicorn in daemon mode has no log file configured.
.TP
.I db.sqlite3
SQLite database (development backend).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the server was started or was already running.
Non-zero when bootstrap,
.B migrate
or the server launch fails.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
DJANGO_ENV=production RUNLOGDB_HOST=0.0.0.0 ./start\-mu2e\-rundb\-viewer
\&./start\-mu2e\-rundb\-viewer          # development mode on 127.0.0.1:8000
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR stop\-mu2e\-rundb\-viewer (1),
.BR bootstrap\-mu2e\-rundb\-viewer (1),
.BR start\-mu2edaq\-runlog\-db.sh (1),
.BR mu2edaq\-runlog\-db.yaml (5),
.BR mu2edaq\-runlog\-db (7)
